\section{Numerical certificates: what they establish and what they do not}
\label{sec:study-certificates}

The analytic derivations define the inequality and the exact relationships
between its operands. Numerical work has several different roles: testing
whether a proposed inequality is plausible, finding a candidate witness,
validating that witness over a declared domain, and checking that the domain
really covers the shipping histories. Only their correctly scoped composition
can establish the final theorem. ``The solver returned success'' is not that
composition.

\subsection{Four kinds of evidence}
\begin{description}
\item[Exact identity or analytic bound.]
A symbolic polynomial identity, rational coefficient check, determinant
argument or proved physical-history bound applies to all operands satisfying
its stated premises. For example the Cayley residual identity is universal
within its chart. It does not prove that every shipping prefix remains in
that chart or that its energy decreases.
\item[Point diagnostic.]
A native replay, tangent product, generalized eigenvalue, high-precision
recomputation or finite accepted-service audit describes the measured states
and source histories. It can falsify a universal assertion with a legal
counterexample, identify a limiting direction, or justify investigating an
architecture. Positive observations do not establish a uniform bound.
\item[Validated inequality certificate.]
A retained witness with exact rational or outward-rounded interval checks
proves a specified inequality over its full declared set. Examples include a
positive-definiteness witness, a lower bound on an information Gramian, an
LDLT pivot enclosure, a finite-increment quadratic inequality, or a prefix
transport bound. A local certificate proves only its own inequality on its
own covered branches; it is not automatically a complete-source certificate.
\item[Source/runtime coverage and composition.]
A separate argument binds the complete continuous BRMM and BIAS families,
all admitted event branches, actual parameter ancestry and target arithmetic
to the certified relations. It must preserve the same successors and memories
across words and establish indefinite domain membership. A finite coverage
sample or a test of the certificate checker is not this universal argument.
\end{description}

\subsection{What the measured $\rho$ actually is}
For a represented tangent word $A_w$, a common diagnostic is
\begin{equation}
 \rho_w^{\rm point}=
 \lambda_{\max}\!\left(
 Z^{\top}A_w^{\top}M(P_{\rm after})A_wZ,
 Z^{\top}M(P_{\rm before})Z\right).
 \label{eq:study-point-rho}
\end{equation}
$Z$ injects the canonical unsupplied initial coordinates. \emph{All output
rows} of $A_wZ$ remain, including active bias corrections. Both endpoint
metrics come from the same prescribed storage law; they are not fitted
separately to make this ratio small. The generalized eigenvector identifies
the most costly direction, and operation-by-operation energy changes show
where the margin is consumed.

The retained quiet, magnetically serviced native experiment measured a worst
local tangent ratio $0.9771585509$ across nine consecutive-window measurements
covering H18, A21 and an actual H18-to-A21 release. Its covariance, tuner,
frontend and clocks were carried from construction without intermediate
reseeding. This supports keeping the compatible storage law as a candidate.
It is \emph{not} a source-uniform finite-error $\rho$, a certified interval
budget, or proof of startup for all histories. The experiment's zero nominal
residual is essential to the tangent construction; nonzero residuals require
their actual gain/reset dependence. A 60-digit terminal calculation checks
conditioning, not outward coverage of all possible trajectories.

The accepted-service regime comparison similarly measures a finite set of
windows. Slower attempted callback schedules used as stress tests are outside
the retained 40 ms call profile, even when their finite information audits
succeed. Neither a spectral radius below one nor an inverse-covariance ratio
below one can replace the required coercivity and retention proof. In
particular, unobserved covariance growth can reduce its inverse weight while
physical error is neutral or growing.
