\section{Proof status, dependency order, and continuation}
\label{sec:study-status}

\subsection{Retained results versus controlling gaps}
The exact finite measurement descriptors, masked held-covariance algebra,
true-bias family bounds, prescribed storage law, qualitative finite-SPD
coercivity lemma and conditional comparison theorem are retained ingredients.
The ungauged unipotent example is a retained negative result. Positive quiet
word ratios remain diagnostics. None of those facts closes all the premises
of Theorem~\ref{thm:study-tail-comparison} for the shipping filter.

The finite-master inventory keeps eleven named qualifications. At the source
snapshot of this study, rows 1, 3, 4, 5, 10 and 11 are open; the other five are
component results under their explicit execution premises. This is not a
percentage of the theorem completed. The controlling work groups naturally as
follows.
\begin{description}
\item[Startup and entry.]
Resolve universal startup reachability (or keep the explicitly weaker
history-dependent capture hypothesis); finish initialization, startup supplies
and the actual rounded entry composition. The reached candidate bad tail
requires its rounding and indefinite wrapper argument, not a larger timeout.
\item[Whole-target and all-event safety.]
Qualify the compiler/library/Eigen call graph and floating environment; prove
bounds and totality for carried MEKF state, bias, covariance, normalization and
solves. Component frontend bounds alone do not establish the whole estimator.
\item[Complete same-history relation.]
Attach the true physical and BIAS history, startup roots, pending yaw,
calibration, quaternion lower shell and every rounded CORE/hybrid successor
to the finite word. Preserve actual applied tuning and one persistent origin.
\item[Information and centre dynamics.]
Prove the physical gravity quotient and centre coupling for moving sources;
retain accepted informative service as a clearly stated hypothesis or establish
its deployment membership. Attempted calls cannot replace it.
\item[Finite-error dissipation and retention.]
Prove indefinite finite-SPD membership, the nonlinear complete-word inequality
for all three bias families and H18/A21 edges, every-prefix basin/clock
retention, and the useful ultimate bound. Source-uniform finite errors and
nonzero motion are not covered by quiet zero-residual tangents.
\end{description}
The original track's canonical P3 usefulness threshold remains $10^{-18}$.
Original P4/P5 and the three ALT PASS flags must remain independently gated;
no editorial reorganization promotes them.

\subsection{A falsifiable order of work}
First attach a complete source/runtime relation before attempting a universal
storage certificate. In parallel, resolve startup reachability as its own
question, with the actual reached bad state rather than an invented seed.
For the selected Live architecture, test nonzero-motion finite-error words
with actual accepted and rejected events at retained cadence, report the
limiting direction and the gravity-fibre/centre coupling, and compare against
the fixed compatible storage law. Only then attempt rigorous enclosure where
a quantitative margin makes it plausible. Validate domain and prefix retention,
compose the tail theorem, and finally attach the startup conclusion with its
correct quantifiers. Failure at any stage is evidence to analyze, not a reason
to weaken the physical domain or bypass a gate.

\subsection{Reproduction and navigation}
The following commands run from the repository root. The native diagnostic
requires the Eigen/build dependencies; its output remains diagnostic. The
provenance command checks evidence lineage, not a new stability inequality.
\begin{quote}\small\ttfamily
PYTHONPATH=.:tools/stability OPENBLAS\_NUM\_THREADS=1 python3 -m\\
\hspace*{1em}tools.stability.ou3\_alt\_contraction.carried\_storage\_rho\_diagnostic\\
\hspace*{1em}--work /tmp/ou3-alt-carried-storage\\
\hspace*{1em}--output /tmp/ou3-alt-carried-storage.json
\end{quote}
\begin{quote}\small\ttfamily
python3 tools/ou\_evidence\_contract.py --check --study all
\end{quote}
For the current executable obligation inventory and proof continuation use
\path{docs/ou3-alt-main-handover.md} and
\path{docs/ou3-alt-proof-plan.md}; for the independent original route use
\path{docs/ou3-brmm-main-handover.md}. The research ledger
\path{docs/ou3-proof-research-state.md} distinguishes theorem, method,
enclosure, conditioning and implementation failures. The detailed sections
that follow supply the retained mathematics, not a chronological list of PRs.
